                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Heart of Ember is an amateurish casual little RPG.\n\nSure, this part-time project could use better quality control (text escapes its boxes, you can get stuck in scenery, and you need to scroll to see major options like \"Exit\"), the stats are rather simplistic (we don't get to distribute ability points when we level), the prince is in our party but we can't see him unless we're fighting, the save system (interact with a save point or you won't be saved) and the mostly featureless landscape - all of this makes Heart of Ember an amateur production. But the writing and world-building, with backstory and secrets hinted at (and good BGM), is, while not epic, sufficiently enticing to me to not want to not recommend this game. It's not much of a challenge, but it's [i]nice[/i], and it doesn't feel dumb. Chapter 1 is all you get right now (it ends on a huge cliffhanger), and it takes 1-2 hours to complete.\n\nYou might find the price a tad high for a small amateur production, but if you catch it in a bundle or it is on sale, give it a look.",
